[00:00] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja Beta UI showing "Good afternoon." and a "Get Lifetime for $79" offer.
AUDIO: 'Beta.4 is out and this one is different. macOS is finally here and this update ships more than 15 new features. Let\'s get into it. First feature, macOS. Uja now runs natively on Apple Silicon. Same tools, same interface, same .uja files,'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'nothing was cut for the Mac. Sculpting, painting, splitting, supports, molds, rendering, all of it is there on day one. And Windows and Mac users can pass projects back and forth freely with no'

[00:28] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI demonstrating the "Separate Colors" and "Outline Cut" features on a 3D model.
AUDIO: 'compatibility issues. One thing worth mentioning for the first launch, Uja for Mac is waiting on Apple\'s notarization, which is Apple\'s standard review process for new developer accounts and it\'s in'

[00:41] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'progress right now. Until it clears, macOS will show a warning the first time you open the app. Just click done, go to system settings, privacy and security, and hit open anyway. That\'s it. Uja opens normally from that point on and'

[00:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the notarized build will arrive without needing to reinstall anything. Second feature, AR live. Scan a QR code with your phone and your model appears in your actual room at real printed size through the camera. Walk around it and'

[01:07] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI showing the "AI Generation" panel with an API key input for Tripo.
AUDIO: 'judge the scale for real before you spend a spool printing the wrong size. Nothing to install, runs in the browser over Wi-Fi. Works on Android, iPhone, and any phone. Rescale on desktop and the AR updates on your phone'

[01:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'automatically. Third feature, AI 3D generation. You can now generate 3D models directly inside Uja powered by Tripo. Create a Tripo account, add some credit, 5 to 10 US dollars goes a long'

[01:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'way, generate an API key, paste it into Uja once, and that\'s it. Everything runs inside Uja from there. No browser, no downloads, build straight to your own'

[01:45] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI displaying a generated 3D model of a demon-like creature.
AUDIO: 'account with no markup. Upload a photo or just type what you want. Uja submits the job and drops the finished model straight into your scene ready for print. You choose between clean geometry to paint yourself or a fully colored'

[01:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'model. The exact credit cost shows before you run each generation and your remaining balance is always visible in the panel. And this is just the beginning. We\'re building our own in-house generation model called Waget, planned for the official Auja release.'

[02:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Fourth feature, Decor Studio. A full parametric studio for decorative and functional prints. Every slider updates the mesh live and everything comes out watertight and print ready. Draw the'

[02:25] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI demonstrating the "Decor Studio" with a parametric vase design.
AUDIO: 'silhouette with a profile curve, then shape the body with flutes, ribs, lobes, and twist. Add up to four handles, vertical or pot ear style, rope or braid with full control over placement and how'

[02:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'far they bow out. Dress the walls in relief patterns from the built-in catalog or import your own black and white image and Auja turns it into a repeating relief pattern across the surface. Draw decorative beads and'

[02:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'grooves freehand with curve handles and symmetry or import a PNG and its shape becomes real conforming relief on the vase. Add drain holes with position, size, and rotation control and any vase'

[03:04] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI showing a cactus character model with applied decals in "Decal Studio".
AUDIO: 'becomes a proper planter. And for organizers, build desk organizers, hook racks, and hangers with live compartment divisions in different shapes. And if you want a custom footprint, just import'

[03:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a picture and Auja traces its outline into the organizer shape automatically. Fifth feature, Decal Studio. Three tools in one studio for putting real graphics on real prints. First is colored decals.'

[03:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Import any PNG or JPG, a logo, a label, artwork, and press it onto the surface in full color. Drag it exactly where you want it and if you need the logo as its'

[03:42] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI displaying 3D text "AUDJA" with options for fill and outline styles.
AUDIO: 'own separate piece, a depth cut engraves the pocket and produces a part that fills it exactly. Second is 3D text. Emboss or engrave text directly onto the mesh or build stand-alone text that'

[03:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'stands on the build plate. Full choice of fonts, filled or outline styles, chamfer or rounded bevels, and an optional backing plate. Third is flat art. Import an SVG or AI file or a plain'

[04:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'PNG which Uja traces automatically and it becomes a layered multi-color printable plate. You control the smoothness and thickness of every color'

[04:21] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI demonstrating "Surface Fit" by applying a deer shape onto a curved surface.
AUDIO: 'layer. Sixth feature, surface fit. Any flat mesh, a badge, logo, emblem, or nameplate can now be fitted onto a curved surface. Drop it on the model and it bends to hug the surface underneath.'

[04:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Drag it across and it slides along the curvature refitting live as it moves with a gizmo for rotation and scale. What used to take careful sculpting in another app is now one drag. Seventh'

[04:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'feature, texture studio. Give any model real surface detail. Wood grain, fabric, camo, scales, marble, anything you can find online. Download a texture image, import it into Uja, and apply it exactly'

[05:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'where you want. Paint it on with the brush for precise control or cover whole regions in one click with smart fill, then tune the scale and look until it sits right. Eighth feature, image'

[05:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'relief. Turn any picture into a printable relief. Import a photo or artwork and Uja builds a raised 3D relief from it. Pick the plate shape, set the size and depth, fine-tune the detail, then either stamp it directly'

[05:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'onto an existing model or keep it stand-alone for wall art, plaques, or gifts. Ninth feature, chroma. Turn any image into a printable painting with no AMS required. Chroma breaks your picture'

[05:37] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI showing multiple open windows, including Audja Pro update page and various 3D models.
AUDIO: 'down into a stack of thin filament layers. You pick the colors and number of slots and Uja figures out which color goes where and at what height. Prints on a single nozzle with simple filament'

[05:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'swaps, no purge tower, no waste, just clean layers that blend into the full image. 10th feature, channels. Carve internal tunnels through any mesh, drainage for planters, cable runs,'

[06:03] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI demonstrating "Articulate" by adding joints to a human-like figure.
AUDIO: 'watering tubes, drip towers, or any kind of hollow passage. Drop anchor points on the surface, pull the path inside the model with a gizmo, and Ouija carves a smooth tunnel along it. Self-supporting'

[06:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'teardrop profile that prints cleanly without supports. Adjustable diameter. 11th feature, articulate. Turn any solid character into a jointed posable figure. Mark where the joints go, and Ouija cuts'

[06:28] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the body and builds matching joints in place. Five joint styles to pick from, organic capture, ball link, pin fork, knee hinge, and body ball. Each with its own clearance control and mirror joints'

[06:40] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI showing "Boolean Operations" with a cylinder and a cube.
AUDIO: 'across an axis, so both arms come out identical. Honest note, this is a first version and a solid foundation will keep improving in every update based on what your actual prints tell us. Print it, pose it, and let us know what worked and'

[06:54] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what didn\'t. 12th feature, Boolean operations. Assign, union, subtract, intersect, or exclude to any object. Pick a base mesh and see the result live before you commit. 10 ready-made shapes to drop in and reshape live. Clearance'

[07:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'slider, so printed parts actually fit. Auto mesh repair and colors survive the cut. 13th feature, outline cut. No longer 2D only. A new 3D surface mode lets you click points directly on the'

[07:23] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI demonstrating "Connector Keys" on an avocado keychain model.
AUDIO: 'model in the viewport. The curve hugs the surface and stays put while you orbit, so you can wrap a cut around geometry no flat view could reach. Both modes now have symmetry, too. Mirror your points into one symmetric curve or'

[07:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cut twin mirrored pieces in a single pass. 14th feature, connector keys. The connector family now has 12 shapes with the new snap latch, a flat cantilever clip that prints lying flat for maximum'

[07:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'strength and clicks parts together with no glue. The barbed tip locks into a ledge inside the cavity and placing connectors got more accurate, too. Alongside the pin preview in Amber'

[08:01] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI showing the "Export" menu with options for OBJ and GLB texture images.
AUDIO: 'Ghost, now shows the exact envelope your clearance setting will carve, so you see the real printed fit before you cut, not a guess. 15th feature, painted models from Blender, ZBrush, and Substance'

[08:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Painter. Import an OBJ or GLB with textures and the colors show up instantly. Uja converts the UV texture into real vertex colors on the mesh the'

[08:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'moment it loads. Sculpt and paint in whatever 3D app you use, bring it into Uja for print prep and every color is intact, ready for AMS painting separation, and slicer export. 16th'

[08:38] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja Pro updates webpage highlighting "17 New Languages" and "18 A More Comfortable Viewport".
AUDIO: 'update, offline. Sign in once and you\'re good. Lifetime license holders stay signed in for 90 days with no connection needed at all, beta users for 14 days. Open Uja in a workshop with no Wi-Fi, on'

[08:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'a plane, anywhere, it starts instantly and your license just works, renewing quietly in the background whenever you\'re back online. 17th feature, 25 languages. Uja now speaks 25 languages.'

[09:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'In this update, Russian, Ukrainian, Polish, Swedish, Norwegian, Estonian, Greek, Hebrew, Vietnamese, Indonesian, Filipino, Hindi, Spanish Argentina, and'

[09:18] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI demonstrating "Outline Cut" on a mushroom-shaped model.
AUDIO: 'Spanish Mexico. Complete translations of the entire interface, switchable anytime in preferences. 18th update, a more comfortable viewport. A few quality of'

[09:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'life improvements that make everyday work smoother. View clip in the color painter cuts away everything between you and the model so you can paint places a brush could never reach before. Cross-section view can now fill the cut'

[09:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'face with a solid color so slicing through a model shows a clean face instead of a hollow interior. Orbit below the build plate and it hides itself so you can inspect the underside and comes back when you rise above it.'

[09:56] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI showing a smooth, round character model.
AUDIO: 'Right click a filament slot to swap it with any other or drag one onto another to merge its paint. Reorganizing a palette mid-project takes seconds and zoom to cursor now truly zooms toward'

[10:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your cursor and a new alt plus left click orbit means you can always rotate even when zoomed in all the way. Now for the fixes. First fix, sculpt smoothing. Smoothing a model in sculpt mode and'

[10:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'going back to the main workspace used to silently throw the smoothing away. The surface just snapped back like you never touched it. That\'s fixed now. What you sculpt is what you keep every time. Second fix, heavy models. The paintbrush'

[10:35] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja Pro updates webpage detailing "Heavy Models: Smoother Painting and Imports" and "Project Saves Keep Your Whole Cut Workflow".
AUDIO: 'used to freeze the whole app the second you hovered over a large mesh. That stall is gone. Brushwork on big sculpts is dramatically more responsive now. Importing large OBJ and STL files is'

[10:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'smoother, too. Viewport stays fluid while you work with heavyweight models. Third fix, project saves. Cut heavy projects now reopen exactly as you left them. The link between a source model'

[11:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and its cut parts is saved inside the project. So SRC and CUT badges are still there and still connected when you reopen. The assembled arrangement from a blade split is saved, too. So the'

[11:13] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja UI demonstrating "Outline Cut" on a blue, vase-like object.
AUDIO: 'assemble preview is right where you left it. And there\'s a new export option that saves only the cut results. One merged STL or separate files skipping the source meshes so getting parts to the'

[11:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'slicer is faster. Fourth fix, socket separation rebuilt under the hood. Cuts compute faster, the plug and cavity come out cleaner and actually match each other, and the controls, depth, taper,'

[11:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'slide, mouth gap all respond the way you expect. Big separations that used to take forever now just happen. And one more thing, we added a feature requests page on the website. If something in Auja is slowing you down or missing'

[11:50] [scene:ui]
VISUAL: Audja Pro "Tell us what's missing." feature request page.
AUDIO: 'entirely, tell us. The team reads every single request, and the best ones ship. When you send one, include a concrete example, the model, the printer, the colors, what you\'re doing today to work around it, and a reference or screenshot'

[12:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'if you have one. The sharpest ideas come from people actually standing at a printer. So, if that\'s you, we want to hear it. And honestly, none of this would exist without the community. Every piece of feedback, every bug report, every request, it all went into beta.4,'

[12:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and it\'s what keeps pushing this forward. More tutorials are coming, too, in multiple languages, so stay tuned for that. Thank you, genuinely. Means a lot.'
